From f391a93ac6c065af183a70fde7a724b68e97b260 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henry Essinghigh <henry@essinghigh.dev>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:46:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: octeon-wdt: report the full heartbeat timeout

The driver implements a long watchdog heartbeat using shorter hardware
periods. Report the complete heartbeat through watchdog_device.timeout,
not the hardware interrupt period, and update it when setting a timeout.

Otherwise WDIOC_SETTIMEOUT returns the initial five-second period after
programming a thirty-second heartbeat. A subsequent initialization by
procd reuses that value and reduces the heartbeat to five seconds, equal
to its default keepalive interval.

Signed-off-by: Henry Essinghigh <henry@essinghigh.dev>
---
 drivers/watchdog/octeon-wdt-main.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/watchdog/octeon-wdt-main.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/octeon-wdt-main.c
@@ -462,6 +462,7 @@ static int octeon_wdt_set_timeout(struct
 		return -1;
 
 	octeon_wdt_calc_parameters(t);
+	wdog->timeout = t;
 
 	if (disable)
 		return 0;
@@ -555,7 +556,7 @@ static int __init octeon_wdt_init(void)
 
 	pr_info("Initial granularity %d Sec\n", timeout_sec);
 
-	octeon_wdt.timeout	= timeout_sec;
+	octeon_wdt.timeout	= heartbeat;
 	octeon_wdt.max_timeout	= UINT_MAX;
 
 	watchdog_set_nowayout(&octeon_wdt, nowayout);
